16. MODEL REPLACEMENT MUST NOT CAUSE MEMORY SHOCK

Example:

Today:
CNS + Model A

Tomorrow:
CNS + Model B

Model B should receive the relevant CNS context, knowledge, rules and state required to continue the work.

The new model should not need to “become” CNS.

It plugs into CNS.


---

17. MEMORY IMPORT / EXPORT

Memory must be portable.

Possible purposes:

Backup

Migration

New server

New CNS installation

Disaster recovery

Model transition

Knowledge transfer


Conceptually:

CNS Memory
    ↓
EXPORT
    ↓
Backup / Transfer
    ↓
NEW CNS
    ↓
IMPORT
    ↓
Continuity restored

This also provides a foundation for onboarding future models.

Important distinction:

> Memory transfer is not automatically model training.



Initially CNS should achieve continuity through memory, context, retrieval and system rules.

Actual model fine-tuning/training can be added later as a separate capability.


