The fundamental separation is:

Models think.

Memory remembers.

Tools provide capabilities.

Bots perform assigned work.

Trading engines execute deterministic financial logic.

Connections connect outside systems.

Agents perform workflows.

CNS coordinates and governs everything.

The user remains in control.


---

37. FINAL IMPLEMENTATION RULE

> Build the control-plane interfaces and subsystem boundaries first. Do not prematurely hard-code the detailed internal settings of future subsystems. When each subsystem is implemented, create its own detailed specification and connect it to the established CNS control plane.



This allows CNS to grow from:

four trading Bots → additional financial Bots → new models → new providers → new tools → new external systems

without redesigning the foundation.


---

FINAL ARCHITECTURAL IDEA

> CNS should be a complete system by itself, but never a closed system.



It should be possible to:

replace the brain,

add another brain,

change model homes,

add capabilities,

add Bots,

connect brokers,

connect market-data providers,

connect external services,

add future harnesses,

migrate memory,

use CLI,

use GUI,

use chat,

use voice,


without rebuilding CNS from scratch.

The model is replaceable.

The provider is replaceable.

The Bot is replaceable.

The connection is replaceable.

The interface is replaceable.

The memory remains CNS's continuity.

The control plane remains the common nervous system.

